body:
+1 (non-binding)

I verified:
- checksums and signatures for the ASF artifacts;
- signing key and tag/commit identity;
- archive safety, LICENSE/NOTICE, RAT, and source-only contents;
- source artifact equivalence to the tag and commit;
- build from source;
- unit tests (3969 passed, 3 skipped);
- S3, ADLS, and GCS test targets;
- wheel metadata, RECORD, licenses, platform tags, native architectures, and provenance.

The environment-sensitive integration failures and the distribution/module version distinction are non-blocking in my assessment. Cross-platform wheels were inspected statically; I did not execute every wheel on its target platform.

The source artifact is ready for release from my review.

+1 (non-binding)

I verified:

- the source artifact checksum, signature, signing key, and signed annotated tag;
- that the source archive matches the advertised commit and contains the expected LICENSE and NOTICE files;
- RAT and binary license inventory checks;
- the build, unit tests, and integration tests from the downloaded source artifact, including acceptance tests against a real Iceberg REST catalog;
- the signed checksums, contents, licensing, target metadata, and commit provenance of all convenience binaries.

I found no release-blocking issues.
